---
import { url } from "../utils/url";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "@fontsource/noto-serif-devanagari/400.css";
import "@fontsource/noto-serif-devanagari/600.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Inner Journey | Saroj Baral"
  description="A personal reflection on Shiva Bhakti, spiritual inquiry, Sanatana Dharma and the lifelong journey towards self-understanding."
>
  <main class="spiritual-page">
    <section class="spiritual-hero">
      <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="site-container hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="kailash" viewBox="0 0 520 300" role="presentation">
            <defs>
              <linearGradient id="mountainShade" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1">
                <stop offset="0" stop-color="#7186A5" />
                <stop offset="1" stop-color="#263954" />
              </linearGradient>
              <linearGradient id="snowShade" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0.8" y2="1">
                <stop offset="0" stop-color="#F4F1E9" />
                <stop offset="1" stop-color="#AEBBCB" />
              </linearGradient>
            </defs>
            <circle cx="395" cy="65" r="37" fill="#E9D7A6" opacity=".9" />
            <circle cx="410" cy="53" r="34" fill="#101B2D" />
            <path d="M18 275 147 132l45 48L278 48l74 106 42-43 108 164Z" fill="url(#mountainShade)" />
            <path d="m278 48 31 45-25-10-19 23-17-18-22 20Z" fill="url(#snowShade)" />
            <path d="m147 132 29 31-26-8-19 19-14-18Z" fill="#D6DDE5" opacity=".9" />
            <path d="m352 154 29-43 24 31-23-10-15 17Z" fill="#D6DDE5" opacity=".75" />
            <path d="M0 276h520" stroke="#D6B878" stroke-width="1" opacity=".45" />
          </svg>
          <span class="art-caption">A quiet symbol of stillness · मौन र स्थिरताको प्रतीक</span>
        </div>

        <p class="eyebrow">A PERSONAL SPIRITUAL JOURNEY</p>
        <p class="hero-mantra" lang="sa">ॐ नमः शिवाय</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title">The journey within.</h1>
        <p class="hero-subtitle" lang="ne">भक्ति, जिज्ञासा र आत्मबोधतर्फको निरन्तर यात्रा।</p>
        <p class="hero-intro">
          I am a seeker on a path shaped by devotion to Shiva, curiosity about the wisdom of Sanatana Dharma,
          and the quiet pursuit of self-understanding. This is not a declaration of spiritual attainment;
          it is a reflection of a journey that continues to unfold.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-intro nepali" lang="ne">
          शिवभक्तिको आधार, सनातन दर्शनप्रतिको जिज्ञासा र आत्मचिन्तनको अभ्याससँगै अघि बढिरहेको एउटा व्यक्तिगत यात्रा।
          यो कुनै सिद्धि वा उपलब्धिको घोषणा होइन; सिक्दै, बुझ्दै र आफूलाई चिन्दै अघि बढ्ने निरन्तर प्रयास हो।
        </p>
        <a class="scroll-cue" href="#foundation">Explore the journey <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section" id="foundation">
      <div class="site-container narrow">
        <p class="section-index">01 / THE FOUNDATION</p>
        <h2>Shiva at the centre.</h2>
        <p class="section-nepali" lang="ne">आराध्य शिव, दृष्टिकोणमा समन्वय।</p>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Lord Shiva is at the heart of my devotional outlook. I am drawn to the stillness, depth and
            many-sided symbolism associated with Shiva — the ascetic and the householder, the dissolver
            and the source of renewal, the silence beyond words and the presence felt within life.
          </p>
          <p lang="ne">
            मेरो उपासनाको केन्द्रमा भगवान् शिव हुनुहुन्छ। वैराग्य र गृहस्थ जीवन, संहार र पुनःसृजन,
            मौन र चेतना — शिवतत्त्वका यी विविध आयामले मलाई भक्ति मात्र होइन, चिन्तन र आत्मअन्वेषणतर्फ पनि प्रेरित गर्छन्।
          </p>
          <p>
            My approach is Shiva-centred, while remaining respectful of the wider devotional traditions
            of Sanatana Dharma. I see the reverence offered to the Divine in its many forms as an invitation
            to understand unity without dismissing the richness of different paths.
          </p>
          <p lang="ne">
            मेरो दृष्टि शिवकेन्द्रित भए पनि सनातन परम्पराका अन्य देवस्वरूप र उपासना पद्धतिप्रति श्रद्धा राख्छु।
            विविध मार्गको मौलिकतालाई सम्मान गर्दै तिनमा निहित आध्यात्मिक एकत्व बुझ्ने प्रयास नै मेरो दृष्टिकोण हो।
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-line">
          <span lang="sa">शिवोऽहम्</span>
          <p>A contemplative expression to explore — not a claim of personal realisation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section alternate">
      <div class="site-container">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-index">02 / THE WAY OF PRACTICE</p>
          <h2>Devotion as a daily orientation.</h2>
          <p class="section-nepali" lang="ne">भक्ति केवल कर्मकाण्ड होइन, जीवनलाई हेर्ने एउटा भाव पनि हो।</p>
        </div>
        <div class="practice-grid">
          <article class="practice-card">
            <span class="card-symbol" aria-hidden="true">ॐ</span>
            <h3>Bhakti <span lang="ne">भक्ति</span></h3>
            <p>
              Cultivating a sincere relationship with the Divine through remembrance, prayer, reverence
              and gratitude. The value lies not in display, but in the inward attitude behind the practice.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="practice-card">
            <span class="card-symbol" aria-hidden="true">जप</span>
            <h3>Sadhana <span lang="ne">साधना</span></h3>
            <p>
              Returning to a chosen discipline with patience and consistency. A practice is meaningful
              when it gradually shapes attention, conduct and the way one meets everyday life.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="practice-card">
            <span class="card-symbol" aria-hidden="true">ధ్యान</span>
            <h3>Contemplation <span lang="ne">आत्मचिन्तन</span></h3>
            <p>
              Making room for silence, observation and honest self-questioning — looking beyond habit
              and appearance towards a clearer understanding of the self.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="privacy-note">
          The details of personal worship and routine are kept private. What is shared here is the
          direction and meaning of the journey, not a public account of private practice.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="site-container narrow">
        <p class="section-index">03 / THE FIELD OF INQUIRY</p>
        <h2>Learning is part of the path.</h2>
        <p class="section-nepali" lang="ne">श्रद्धासँगै प्रश्न, अध्ययन र विवेक पनि आवश्यक छन्।</p>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Devotion and inquiry need not stand apart. I am interested in exploring the philosophical
            foundations of Sanatana Dharma: reading, comparing interpretations, understanding context
            and asking what a teaching means beyond its familiar words.
          </p>
          <p lang="ne">
            मेरो लागि श्रद्धा र जिज्ञासा एकअर्काका विरोधी होइनन्। सनातन धर्मका दार्शनिक आधारहरू अध्ययन गर्ने,
            विभिन्न व्याख्यालाई बुझ्ने, सन्दर्भ खोज्ने र शास्त्रीय वचनको गहिरो अर्थमाथि विचार गर्ने रुचि छ।
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="study-list">
          <div class="study-item">
            <span class="study-number">01</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Shaiva thought <span lang="ne">शैव दर्शन</span></h3>
              <p>Shiva's nature, symbolism, worship traditions and the philosophical visions within Shaiva thought.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="study-item">
            <span class="study-number">02</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Vedanta and self-inquiry <span lang="ne">वेदान्त र आत्मविचार</span></h3>
              <p>Exploring questions of self, consciousness, reality and liberation through different Vedantic perspectives.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="study-item">
            <span class="study-number">03</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Cosmology and the Tattvas <span lang="ne">सृष्टि र तत्त्वचिन्तन</span></h3>
              <p>Learning about creation, the five divine acts and the frameworks through which Indian philosophies describe existence.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="study-item">
            <span class="study-number">04</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Scripture, stotra and meaning <span lang="ne">शास्त्र, स्तोत्र र भावार्थ</span></h3>
              <p>Approaching Sanskrit verses through their language, context, devotional feeling and philosophical meaning.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="caution-note">
          I approach these subjects as a learner. Different schools of thought have their own foundations
          and interpretations; understanding them requires patience rather than forcing every teaching
          into a single conclusion.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section alternate">
      <div class="site-container">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-index">04 / SOURCES OF INSPIRATION</p>
          <h2>Learning from those who walked before.</h2>
          <p class="section-nepali" lang="ne">सन्त, आचार्य र साधकका जीवन तथा शिक्षाबाट प्रेरणा।</p>
          <p class="section-intro">
            The lives and teachings of saints, philosophers and spiritual teachers offer different
            windows into devotion, discipline and the search for truth. I approach them as sources
            of reflection and learning, not as a claim of belonging to a particular lineage.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="inspiration-grid">
          <article class="inspiration-card">
            <h3>Adi Shankaracharya</h3>
            <p class="native-name" lang="ne">आदि शङ्कराचार्य</p>
            <p>For the inquiry into non-duality, discernment and the relationship between knowledge and liberation.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="inspiration-card">
            <h3>Goswami Tulsidas</h3>
            <p class="native-name" lang="ne">गोस्वामी तुलसीदास</p>
            <p>For the depth of devotional poetry and the way sacred stories can shape the heart and character.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="inspiration-card">
            <h3>Sant Tukaram</h3>
            <p class="native-name" lang="ne">सन्त तुकाराम</p>
            <p>For simplicity, humility and the directness of heartfelt devotion.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="inspiration-card">
            <h3>Gorakhnath</h3>
            <p class="native-name" lang="ne">गोरखनाथ</p>
            <p>For the contemplative and yogic traditions that explore discipline, awareness and inner transformation.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="inspiration-card">
            <h3>Machhindranath</h3>
            <p class="native-name" lang="ne">मच्छिन्द्रनाथ</p>
            <p>For the heritage and spiritual imagination of the Nath tradition.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="inspiration-card">
            <h3>Premanand Maharaj</h3>
            <p class="native-name" lang="ne">प्रेमानन्द महाराज</p>
            <p>For contemporary reflections on devotion, remembrance and the sincerity of spiritual life.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="site-container narrow">
        <p class="section-index">05 / WHERE WORLDS MEET</p>
        <h2>When learning becomes creation.</h2>
        <p class="section-nepali" lang="ne">अध्ययन, प्रविधि र भक्तिको एउटा सानो संगम।</p>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            My background is in engineering and technology, and I enjoy bringing structure to ideas.
            That inclination has also found a place in my spiritual interests: organising prayers and
            stotras, studying their meanings, and creating a digital space where devotional material
            can be approached with clarity and care.
          </p>
          <p lang="ne">
            मेरो इन्जिनियरिङ र प्रविधिसँगको पृष्ठभूमिले विचारलाई व्यवस्थित गर्ने बानी दिएको छ।
            यही रुचि आध्यात्मिक अध्ययनमा पनि जोडिएको छ — प्रार्थना र स्तोत्रलाई सङ्ग्रह गर्ने,
            तिनको भावार्थ बुझ्ने र अध्ययन सामग्रीलाई सरल तथा व्यवस्थित रूपमा प्रस्तुत गर्ने प्रयासमा।
          </p>
          <p>
            It is a small personal undertaking, not a religious institution or a source of spiritual
            authority. Its purpose is simply to support learning, remembrance and thoughtful engagement
            with the traditions that inspire me.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing-section">
      <div class="site-container closing-inner">
        <div class="closing-mark" aria-hidden="true">ॐ</div>
        <p class="section-index">THE JOURNEY CONTINUES</p>
        <h2>Not a destination.<br />A lifelong unfolding.</h2>
        <p class="closing-nepali" lang="ne">सिकाइ जारी छ। खोज जारी छ। यात्रा जारी छ।</p>
        <p>
          I do not present myself as a guru, an authority or someone who has arrived at the end
          of the path. I am a learner — trying to bring devotion, discernment and sincerity into
          the same journey. There is always more to understand, more to question and more room to grow.
        </p>
        <p class="closing-verse" lang="sa">असतो मा सद्गमय । तमसो मा ज्योतिर्गमय । मृत्योर्माऽमृतं गमय ॥</p>
        <p class="verse-translation">Lead me from the unreal to the real, from darkness to light, from mortality to immortality.</p>
        <p class="closing-signoff" lang="ne">ॐ शान्तिः शान्तिः शान्तिः</p>
        <nav class="page-links" aria-label="Page navigation">
          <a href={url("/about")}>Back to About</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <a href={url("/contact")}>Get in touch</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .spiritual-page {
    --sp-bg: #0b1424;
    --sp-panel: #111e31;
    --sp-panel-soft: #15243a;
    --sp-text: #dce3ec;
    --sp-muted: #aab6c6;
    --sp-gold: #d9b978;
    --sp-line: rgba(217, 185, 120, .23);
    background: var(--sp-bg);
    color: var(--sp-text);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .site-container {
    width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 48px));
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .narrow { max-width: 790px; }

  .spiritual-hero {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    min-height: 760px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 12%, rgba(56, 78, 111, .32), transparent 48%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, #0b1424 0%, #101d31 70%, #0b1424 100%);
  }

  .hero-glow {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: -1;
    width: 620px;
    height: 620px;
    top: -300px;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgba(217, 185, 120, .07);
    filter: blur(70px);
  }

  .hero-inner {
    max-width: 850px;
    padding-block: 82px 76px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .hero-art { margin: 0 auto 24px; }
  .kailash { display: block; width: min(440px, 86vw); height: auto; margin-inline: auto; }
  .art-caption {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 5px;
    color: #8291a6;
    font-size: .72rem;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
  }

  .eyebrow, .section-index {
    color: var(--sp-gold);
    font-size: .72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: .19em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 20px; }
  .hero-mantra {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--sp-gold);
    font-family: "Noto Serif Devanagari", var(--font-serif, Georgia), serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 7vw, 4.3rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .hero-title {
    margin: 0;
    color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--font-serif, Georgia), serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 5.1rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -.045em;
    line-height: 1.08;
  }

  .hero-subtitle, .section-nepali, .closing-nepali {
    color: var(--sp-gold);
    font-family: "Noto Serif Devanagari", var(--font-serif, Georgia), serif;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .hero-subtitle { margin: 20px 0 22px; font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.3vw, 1.22rem); }
  .hero-intro {
    max-width: 690px;
    margin: 0 auto 13px;
    color: #c2ccda;
    font-size: 1.04rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
  }
  .hero-intro.nepali { color: #aeb9c9; font-family: "Noto Serif Devanagari", var(--font-serif, Georgia), serif; font-size: .98rem; }
  .scroll-cue {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 30px;
    color: var(--sp-gold);
    font-size: .82rem;
    letter-spacing: .06em;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .scroll-cue span { font-size: 1.1rem; transition: transform .2s ease; }
  .scroll-cue:hover span { transform: translateY(4px); }

  .content-section { padding: 104px 0; background: var(--sp-bg); }
  .content-section.alternate { background: #0e192a; }
  .section-index { margin: 0 0 19px; }
  .content-section h2, .closing-section h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: #f5f3ee;
    font-family: var(--font-serif, Georgia), serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.8vw, 3.35rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -.035em;
    line-height: 1.16;
  }
  .section-nepali { margin: 14px 0 30px; font-size: 1rem; }
  .prose { color: #c1ccda; font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.9; }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 20px; }
  .prose p[lang="ne"] { color: #b8c3d1; font-family: "Noto Serif Devanagari", var(--font-serif, Georgia), serif; font-size: .98rem; line-height: 2; }

  .principle-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 22px;
    margin-top: 38px;
    padding: 21px 24px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--sp-gold);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .035);
  }
  .principle-line span {
    color: var(--sp-gold);
    font-family: "Noto Serif Devanagari", serif;
    font-size: 1.65rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .principle-line p { margin: 0; color: var(--sp-muted); font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.6; }

  .section-heading { max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 38px; }
  .section-intro { max-width: 700px; color: #b9c5d4; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; }
  .practice-grid, .inspiration-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
  .practice-card, .inspiration-card {
    padding: 27px 25px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(190, 204, 224, .12);
    border-radius: 13px;
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(255,255,255,.045), rgba(255,255,255,.015));
  }
  .card-symbol { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 18px; color: var(--sp-gold); font-family: "Noto Serif Devanagari", serif; font-size: 1.8rem; }
  .practice-card h3, .inspiration-card h3, .study-item h3 {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    color: #f0eee8;
    font-family: var(--font-serif, Georgia), serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .practice-card h3 span { margin-left: 5px; color: var(--sp-gold); font-family: "Noto Serif Devanagari", serif; font-size: .9rem; }
  .practice-card p, .inspiration-card p:not(.native-name) { margin: 0; color: #aebaca; font-size: .91rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .privacy-note, .caution-note {
    margin: 25px 0 0;
    padding: 16px 19px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sp-line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #b8c3d1;
    font-size: .88rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .study-list { margin-top: 35px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(190, 204, 224, .13); }
  .study-item { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 48px 1fr; gap: 18px; padding: 25px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(190, 204, 224, .13); }
  .study-number { color: var(--sp-gold); font-family: var(--font-serif, Georgia), serif; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .study-item h3 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .study-item h3 span { color: var(--sp-gold); font-family: "Noto Serif Devanagari", serif; font-size: .9rem; }
  .study-item p { margin: 0; color: #aebaca; font-size: .94rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .caution-note { border-color: rgba(190, 204, 224, .12); background: rgba(255,255,255,.025); }

